  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved the best result so far (acc 0.650, F1 0.628), a large jump over singleprofile scvi_n200 (0.520). This confirms multiprofile + avgpool is highly beneficial. However, we have no data on whether transformer aggregation could further improve upon avgpool in this setting. Question: config_006 changes only the aggregation method (avgpool → transformer) while keeping the same encoder (scvi_n200), profile setting (multiprofile), and modality (rna_only), isolating the aggregation effect. Why this is the best next step: It is a single-variable extension of our strongest result, directly testing whether a more expressive aggregation can push performance higher. The answer will inform the aggregation choice for all subsequent multimodal experiments (configs 018-051), making it highly informative for the remaining search. It balances exploitation (building on the best config) with exploration (testing an untested aggregation in the multiprofile regime)."
